        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the walkthrough, we found leakage on the following items:

-Rear doors seal around the doorknob

-Receptacles

-Electrical panel

-Header joist

-Fireplace

-Woodstove chimney

-Bathroom fan (main floor)

The installation of weather strippings, the insulation of the main walls by outside and the replacement of the bathroom fans, would help to increase the airtightness of your home and reduce air leakage. Unfortunately, there is no much to do to seal the wood stove and fireplace. 

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the moment of the assessment the insulation of the main walls was R-12. We recommend adding insulation to reach the city of Whitehorse standard of R-28.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the moment of the evaluation, the attic insulation was R-40. We recommend adding some insulation to reach the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. Attic insulation protects your home against heat loss caused by the stack effect in winter and against the excessive heat transfer from the attic in the living space in the summertime. </ceilings>
                <foundation>We recommend to extend the insulation of the main walls on the basement walls. At least for the pony wall. If possible, increasing the insulation against the concrete wall will contribute to reducing the thermal bridging effect which brings cold by conduction inside your home. Adding insulation will also contribute to making the basement more comfortable. </foundation>
                <Renewables>For any questions concernings the rebates and the programs about solar energy, please follow the link below to get more information:

https://yukon.ca/en/renewable-energy-rebate#eligible-renewable-systems



PLEASE NOTE: The photovoltaic suggested system, is based on the installation of 6 panels. This is only for suggestion purposes, the system might be composed of more than the suggested system.

</Renewables>
                <AdditionalComments>The depressurization test performed as shown a high risk of combustion gas spillage. Therefore, we recommend verifying your carbon monoxide detectors regularly.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
